From 93ad288a381a3689bb59c608de2cf2ac2fa1e0f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ed <edimoldovan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:34:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] soc: apple: aop: T6050 setup port and firmware DMA
 window

apple,t6050-aop with T8140's configuration (EPIC v4, endpoints 0x20-0x23
and 0x2b required), and a log line with the number of AFK endpoints
started. On J714c: RTKit protocol version 12, 13 AFK endpoints started.

The T6050 AOP firmware (pitayaOS, mac17jaop) boots the way T8140's does,
with two things this driver did not do for it:

- host buffers must lie in the DRAM range its cL4 config allows,
  IOVA 0x10040078000..0x20000000000 on dart-aop stream 0. A buffer
  elsewhere makes the firmware panic on the ioreport request ("range not
  in untypeds (try adjusting .mmio)"), write its crash log and halt
  without a crash message, which looked like AFK silence. The aop node
  needs apple,dma-range <0x110 0 0x10 0> (slot 17, inside the range, as
  on T8140).

- its AFK endpoints answer only after the "setup port" handshake on the
  ASC's second mailbox: ADT /arm-io/aop-exclave-mailbox at 0x2d067c000
  (ASC + 1 GiB + 0x7c000 as on T8140), interrupts 582/585, messages
  through dart-aop stream 1, whose window 0x20000000000 +64 GiB is the
  TRUSTED compartment's DRAM range. The port serves three endpoints
  here (0x20, 0x23, 0x32), not T8140's five: AopHwConfig gains
  setup_endpoints, the setup state waits for that list, and the ALS
  calibration runs only where endpoint 0x21 exists.

Also for this firmware: the crashlog buffer it places itself (endpoint
1, not in its endpoint map) is mapped through AopShmem and not
acknowledged; wake_early_ap in the Rust RTKit binding and early_ap in
the config, the wake order T6050 boots with; EPIC service announcements
logged at info level.

Result on J714c: setup port complete, 13 AFK endpoints up, aop-audio /
aop-audprov / aop-voicetrigger announced.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
[port to integration/aurora (aurora-j716s 6d9f1ec652a6): squashes the
 driver parts of 053f1912e7d5 ("AOP bring-up step 1") and f4427365cc8f;
 the T6050 entry carries this tree's ncal/fw_regions/bootargs fields;
 instead of dropping the placed-buffer echo from rtkit.c for every
 client, the T6050 entry sets placed_buffers and probe uses
 RtKit::new_with_placed_buffers_unacked(), so the other AOPs keep their
 RTKit flags; the T6050 comment describes the setup port it now uses.
 DT and j714c.config hunks are board/tree-specific and dropped.]
